        "evidence": "'arbitrarily large atom' is a quantifier, not inflation.",
        "notes": "RIGOR (minor, reported): the block is titled and framed as CONVERGENCE ('assembles into a single convergent representation', 'the convergence content of the ... combiner'), but what is displayed is the one-step recursion cv(A+1) = w(A) cv(A), whose iterate is the telescoping PRODUCT cv(A) = cv(2) * prod_{j=2}^{A-1} w(j). A product converges only if w(j) -> 1, and no such condition is stated or cited anywhere in the block. Proposed: either state the condition on w that makes the tower converge, or retitle the content as a telescoping/product representation (which is what the last sentence actually says) and reserve 'convergent' for wherever the bound on w is proved. Also verified: the peel levels n_k = 3(A-k+1) do give n_1 = 3A, the full strand count, consistent with beta_atom in H_{3A}(q), and bottoming out at k = A-1 gives n = 6, matching 'the deuteron ... computed directly at H_6'."
      }
